/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  column17_exchanger_design  --  column09's column, unchanged, with its
  CONDENSER and REBOILER designed instead of estimated.

  The flowsheet below is column09's to the last key: the same benzene/toluene
  feed, the same 15 stages, the same reflux, the same tray hydraulics.  What
  changes is system/postDict, and the sheets it writes for the two
  exchangers.  Read column09 first; this case is the next question.

  column09 sizes its condenser and reboiler as A = Q/(U LMTD), with U and the
  LMTD TYPED by the author -- a first estimate, not a design.  Here both are
  DESIGNED on the same route a flowsheet exchanger has (a Kern shell-and-tube
  design: the bundle declared, the tube count solved, U a RESULT of the
  films, the wall and the fouling), and the process side of each is priced by
  a PHASE-CHANGE film instead of a single-phase one:

    * the CONDENSER condenses the overhead on the outside of horizontal
      tubes, cooling water inside: Nusselt's laminar film, the condensate of
      one tube falling on the next (h_1 N^-1/4 at the deepest tier);
    * the REBOILER boils the bottoms as a pool around a tube bundle (a
      kettle), LP steam condensing inside: Rohsenow's nucleate flux, HELD
      UNDER the Zuber critical heat flux.

  NOTHING ABOUT THE PROCESS SIDE IS TYPED.  The temperatures are the
  column's own (the top tray's dew point and the distillate's bubble point;
  the bottoms' bubble point), and every property a film needs -- density,
  viscosity, conductivity, heat capacity, surface tension, latent heat --
  comes from constant/thermoPhysPropDict.  That is why this case's package
  declares LIQUID transport models where column09's declares only a surface
  tension: delete one and the exchanger it prices refuses by name.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

units
(
    {
        name        column17;
        type        distillationColumn;
        in          feed;
        outputs     ( distillate  bottoms );

        operation
        {
            nStages        15;
            feedStage      8;
            refluxRatio    2.0;
            distillateRate 50.0 kmol/h;
            P              1.01325 bar;

            hydraulics
            {
                trayType               sieve;
                traySpacing            0.50;     // m
                weirHeight             0.050;    // m
                holeDiameter           5.0e-3;   // m
                holeAreaFraction       0.10;     // A_holes / A_active
                downcomerAreaFraction  0.12;     // A_downcomer / A_tower
                weirLengthFraction     0.77;     // l_weir / D  (goes with 0.12)
                orificeCoefficient     0.84;     // C_o -- read off the Liebson chart
                floodFraction          0.80;     // design target
                K2                     30.7;     // weep chart at h_w + h_ow ~ 60 mm
            }
        }

        compositionTol   1e-7;
        maxOuterIter     200;
    }
);
